{"v":1,"type":"reverie","id":"rv:9f095ffd3726b7d55f507f3f7c17477eac53b6a4","driving_event":"A clean Node 22.20 Debian environment with Git 2.39 rejected git notes append --no-separator and add --no-stripspace, even though the helper declared only a general Git requirement.","decision":"Append by reading the existing canonical note, concatenating the new canonical line, and replacing the temporary note with git notes add -f -F because this preserves canonical JSONL while using commands available in Git 2.39.","impact":"Each append rewrites the affected note body inside the existing locked compare-and-swap transaction, trading work proportional to that note's size for broader Git compatibility without changing note semantics or concurrency guarantees.","recurrence_control":"The exact JSONL test appends two physical records and asserts byte equality, while CI reruns the complete suite in the Node 22.20 Debian image with Git 2.39.","alternatives":["Construct note trees directly with low-level Git plumbing","Declare a newer minimum Git version","Keep the newer append flags and treat old clients as unsupported"],"sources":[{"relation":"corroborated-by","kind":"commit","ref":"5b92381635e13033dbf57b0cdd5fa2965f0f5e28"},{"relation":"requested-by","kind":"git-email","ref":"contact@atkn.me"}],"supersedes":[],"author_email":"contact@atkn.me","session":"codex:01a0396e-0360-7f01-920d-afcbeff3b194","created_at":"2026-08-25T19:11:08Z"}
